---
import BaseLayout from "../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; PERFORMANCE</div>

      <h1>
        Wait Events
      </h1>

      <p>
        Practical Oracle SQL for understanding database wait activity
        and identifying where sessions are spending time.
      </p>

    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="section resource-section">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="resource-intro">

        <div class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; PERFORMANCE</div>

        <h2>
          Understand where database time is going
        </h2>

        <p>
          Oracle wait events provide important evidence when
          investigating performance. Start with the current
          workload, identify the dominant waits, and then
          correlate them with sessions and SQL.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="resource-grid">


        <article class="resource-block">

          <div class="resource-block__header">
            <div class="resource-block__label">
              01 &middot; SYSTEM WAITS
            </div>

            <h2>
              Review system wait events
            </h2>
          </div>

          <p class="resource-block__description">
            Review wait events accumulating time across the database
            instance. Idle waits are excluded from the result.
          </p>

          <pre><code>SELECT
    event,
    wait_class,
    total_waits,
    ROUND(time_waited / 100, 2) AS time_waited_seconds
FROM v$system_event
WHERE wait_class &lt;&gt; 'Idle'
ORDER BY time_waited DESC;</code></pre>

        </article>


        <article class="resource-block">

          <div class="resource-block__header">
            <div class="resource-block__label">
              02 &middot; SESSION WAITS
            </div>

            <h2>
              Identify sessions currently waiting
            </h2>
          </div>

          <p class="resource-block__description">
            Identify active sessions that are currently waiting and
            inspect the event, wait class and duration.
          </p>

          <pre><code>SELECT
    sid,
    serial#,
    username,
    status,
    event,
    wait_class,
    seconds_in_wait,
    state
FROM v$session
WHERE status = 'ACTIVE'
  AND wait_class &lt;&gt; 'Idle'
ORDER BY seconds_in_wait DESC;</code></pre>

        </article>


        <article class="resource-block">

          <div class="resource-block__header">
            <div class="resource-block__label">
              03 &middot; WAIT CLASSES
            </div>

            <h2>
              Group waits by wait class
            </h2>
          </div>

          <p class="resource-block__description">
            Group system wait activity into broader wait classes to
            understand the type of database pressure involved.
          </p>

          <pre><code>SELECT
    wait_class,
    SUM(total_waits) AS total_waits,
    ROUND(SUM(time_waited) / 100, 2) AS time_waited_seconds
FROM v$system_event
WHERE wait_class &lt;&gt; 'Idle'
GROUP BY wait_class
ORDER BY time_waited_seconds DESC;</code></pre>

        </article>


        <article class="resource-block">

          <div class="resource-block__header">
            <div class="resource-block__label">
              04 &middot; SESSION WAIT TIME
            </div>

            <h2>
              Find sessions by accumulated wait time
            </h2>
          </div>

          <p class="resource-block__description">
            Find sessions with significant accumulated wait time and
            use them as a starting point for deeper investigation.
          </p>

          <pre><code>SELECT
    s.sid,
    s.serial#,
    s.username,
    s.status,
    s.event,
    s.wait_class,
    ROUND(se.time_waited / 100, 2) AS time_waited_seconds
FROM v$session_event se
JOIN v$session s
    ON s.sid = se.sid
WHERE se.wait_class &lt;&gt; 'Idle'
ORDER BY se.time_waited DESC
FETCH FIRST 20 ROWS ONLY;</code></pre>

        </article>


        <article class="resource-block">

          <div class="resource-block__header">
            <div class="resource-block__label">05 &middot; BLOCKING</div>

            <h2>
              Identify sessions involved in blocking
            </h2>
          </div>

          <p class="resource-block__description">
            Identify sessions waiting on another session and inspect
            the blocking relationship during concurrency investigation.
          </p>

          <pre><code>SELECT
    sid,
    serial#,
    username,
    status,
    event,
    wait_class,
    blocking_session,
    blocking_session_status,
    seconds_in_wait
FROM v$session
WHERE blocking_session IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY seconds_in_wait DESC;</code></pre>

        </article>


        <article class="resource-block">

          <div class="resource-block__header">
            <div class="resource-block__label">
              06 &middot; INVESTIGATION
            </div>

            <h2>
              Correlate waits with active sessions
            </h2>
          </div>

          <p class="resource-block__description">
            Combine the wait event with the affected session and SQL
            identifier before moving deeper into the investigation.
          </p>

          <pre><code>SELECT
    s.sid,
    s.serial#,
    s.username,
    s.sql_id,
    s.event,
    s.wait_class,
    s.seconds_in_wait,
    s.state
FROM v$session s
WHERE s.status = 'ACTIVE'
  AND s.wait_class &lt;&gt; 'Idle'
ORDER BY s.seconds_in_wait DESC;</code></pre>

        </article>


      </div>


      <div class="resource-note">

        <div class="eyebrow">ORASOLU TOOLBOX &middot; PERFORMANCE</div><h2>
          A wait event is a clue, not automatically the root cause.
        </h2>

        <p>
          Start with the symptom and workload. Identify the significant
          wait, determine which sessions are affected, correlate those
          sessions with SQL and then investigate the underlying resource
          or contention point.
        </p>

        <p>
          Also distinguish idle waits from waits that represent active
          database work. The same wait event can have different meanings
          depending on the workload and context.
        </p>

      </div>


      <div class="resource-actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/tools/performance/">
          Back to Performance
        </a>

        <a class="resource-actions__link" href="/articles/oracle-wait-events/">
          Read Understanding Oracle Wait Events
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>


<script>
  document.querySelectorAll(".resource-block pre").forEach((pre) => {

    const button = document.createElement("button");

    button.type = "button";
    button.className = "resource-copy-button";
    button.textContent = "Copy";
    button.setAttribute("aria-label", "Copy SQL");

    pre.style.position = "relative";

    button.style.position = "absolute";
    button.style.top = "10px";
    button.style.right = "10px";
    button.style.padding = "5px 9px";
    button.style.border = "1px solid #d1d5db";
    button.style.borderRadius = "5px";
    button.style.background = "#ffffff";
    button.style.color = "#374151";
    button.style.fontFamily = "inherit";
    button.style.fontSize = "0.75rem";
    button.style.cursor = "pointer";
    button.style.zIndex = "2";

    button.addEventListener("click", async () => {

      const code = pre.querySelector("code");

      if (!code) {
        return;
      }

      try {

        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent || "");

        button.textContent = "Copied";

        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);

      } catch {

        button.textContent = "Copy failed";

        window.setTimeout(() => {
          button.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1500);

      }

    });

    pre.appendChild(button);

  });
</script>


<style>
  .resource-section {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 72px;
  }


  .resource-intro {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }


